<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco Dueñas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1810–1884</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco Dueñas was a conservative Salvadoran politician who held the presidency several times between 1851 and 1871. Backed by the Guatemalan dictator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-carrera">Rafael Carrera</a>, who overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerardo-barrios">Gerardo Barrios</a> in 1863, he ruled from 1863 to 1871. He was overthrown by a liberal revolt in 1871, after which liberals held power in El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> permanently.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-duenas.jpg" alt="Francisco Dueñas" width="311" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duenas,_Francisco.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
